hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3272","It was narrated by Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him: If a woman dies, her takfeen will be from her property, and her husband will not be burdened with it."
"3273","Ata said: Hanut and Kafan will be done from the actual wealth of the deceased."
"3274","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: The shroud will be given from the property (of the deceased), and the shroud will be the same as he wore in his lifetime, then the debt will be taken out, and after that the bequest of one-third of the property will be enforced."
"3275","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, used to say: If a man makes a will for someone who is absent, then he should accept that will, and if he is present, then he has the authority to accept it if he wants, and if he wants to leave it."
"3276","Ayyub (Al-Sakhtiyani) narrated that I asked Hasan and Muhammad, may God have mercy on him: What if a man makes a will for someone? Both said: He should accept the will."
"3277","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: If a person makes a will for an absent person and he accepts it, then there is no authority to reject it."
"3278","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: When a person makes a will for someone and he is not present, then the will is presented to him who accepts it, then the person who made the will will not have the authority to appeal."
"3279","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When a man makes a will for a person and he is not present, then it is known that he is dead, in such a case the will will return (to the bequeather)."
"3280","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: When a man bequeaths one-third, one-fourth, or one-fifth of his wealth to his slave, it will be paid from his wealth, and this bequest will count as his freedom."
"3281","Qays (Ibn Abi Hazim) said: It used to be said that a man should be deprived of the blessing of his wealth during his life and spend it well when the time of death comes."
"3282","Abdullah said: Two things are bitter: being stagnant in life and extravagant in death. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is said that one is bitter in life and bitter in death."
"3283","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When a man makes a bequest for someone to be given a share like that of his son, his share will not be fulfilled until the son's share is reduced."
"3284","Narrated by Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him: A man who has three sons, and he bequeaths to a man a share equal to one of them, as if he had four sons, Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: He will be given a fifth share."
"3285","Dawood bin Abi Hind said: We asked Amir (Shaabi may God have mercy on him): A man left two sons and bequeathed that a portion equal to the fortune of one of them should be given to so-and-so, while there are three of them. Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: I will give him a quarter. In some manuscripts it is \"Wasi bal-Ruba\" and in some it is \"Ifti-Bal-Ruba\", that is, he issued a fatwa for a quarter."
"3286","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If a man bequeaths (to someone) equal to the share of one of his heirs, he said: Such (ambiguous) bequest even if it is less than one-third, is not permissible. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This saying is good."
"3287","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: If a man bequeaths one dirham to his slave's wages (or labor) and his wages are six (dirhams), he will be given a sixth."
"3288","Qubaysa (bin Uqbah) said: I heard from Sufyan, he used to say: If (the deceased) decides to give one hundred dirhams to an heir or non-heir, then he said: I will declare all such wills invalid."
"3289","Qazi Shareeh said: It is not permissible for an heir to acknowledge (a will), he said, and Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: It is more correct to acknowledge it at the time of death, which is the first day of the Hereafter and the last day of (departing from) this world."
"3290","Abu Qalaba said: A will is not permissible for an heir."
"3291","Narrated by Hameed: A man whose surname was Abu Thabit, at the time of his death bequeathed to his wife four hundred dirhams of her dowry. Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) justified it."
"3292","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Khajri (RA) said: I was near the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) that was grazing and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders, I heard. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: \"Listen, people! Verily, Allah Ta'ala has determined a share for every owner of right (heir). Now it is not permissible to make a will for an heir.\""
"3293","Narrated by Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, this verse: . . . . .» In [Baqarah: 180/2] Allah commanded that when the time of death approaches, he should make a will for his parents and relatives, then the verse of Surah Nisa: . . . . .» [An-Nisaa: 11/4] I fixed a share for the parents, and fixed a share for each heir from the legacy of the deceased, so there is no will for them anymore, and the will became special only for those who are not heirs due to kinship or any other reason."
"3294","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The wealth of (the deceased) was for the children and the will was special for the parents and relatives, of which Allah canceled what He willed, so He kept the double share of the woman for the man and appointed a sixth and a third share for each of the parents, and appointed an eighth and a fourth share for the wife and a half and a fourth share for the husband."
"3295","It was narrated from Ikramah and Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that this verse: . . . . .» According to [Baqarah: 180/2], the will was ongoing and the verse of inheritance: . . . . .» [Nisa' 11/4] revoked the will for the heirs."
"3296","It is narrated from Hameed that Hasan (may God have mercy on him) was asked: Can a man make a will for his rich brother? He said: Yes, he can do it, even if that brother owns twenty thousand, then said: Or if he owns one hundred thousand, his wealth will not deprive him of this right."
"3297","Hasan and Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, said: A man should say that my sword is for so-and-so, and if he dies, then for so-and-so, and if he also dies, it will return to me."
"3298","Hisham bin Arwa narrated that Arwa said: A man should give a donation to a man and say that it is for you, and if you die, it is for so and so, and if such and such a person also dies, it is for so and so, and if he also dies, it will return to me. Urwa said: As said, the will will be enforced even if there are not a hundred men."
"3299","Shiba bin Hisham Rasbi and Kathir bin Madan both said: We asked Salim bin Abdullah: Does a man make a will for his non-relative? Salim said: As said will be enforced, we said: Hasan, may God have mercy on him, you return such a will to the relatives. Salim strongly criticized this."
"3300","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: When a man makes a bequest for a relative, it is for the nearest of the tribe, and men and women are equal in it."
"3301","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: If a man says: One of my two slaves is free, and he dies before making a decision, then Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: The heirs of the testator will take his place, and the one of the two will be freed."
"3302","It was narrated from Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that a man said during his illness: This much is for so-and-so and so-and-so is so much, and my so-and-so slave is free, and he did not say that if any accident happens to me, then so be it, then he recovered. Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: That slave will remain a slave."
"3303","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said about the person who frees his slave at the time of his death, and he has no wealth other than the slave, and he also has debts on him, Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: According to his worth, he will work hard for the debtors."
"3304","On the authority of Hasan, may God have mercy on him: A man bought a slave for seven hundred dirhams, then freed him and did not pay the price of the slave, nor did he leave any other property. (i.e. he will be freed by paying such a price)."
"3305","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The slave of the guardian (of the deceased) will be freed from only one-third (one-third)."
"3306","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The wise man will be freed from one-third of his wealth."
"3307","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: A slave who is freed after death will be freed from one-third of his property."
"3308","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The wise slave girl and her child will be freed from one-third of the property."
"3309","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The slave will be freed from one-third of the wealth of the deceased."
"3310","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The slave will be freed from the entire wealth of the slave."
"3311","Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: A slave who is freed after death will be freed from his wealth tomorrow. The narrator said: Imam Abu Muhammad Darmi, may God have mercy on him, was asked: What is your opinion? Said: One third will be free from wealth."
"3312","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Do not be a witness to a will until it is recited to you, and do not bear witness to what you do not know."
"3313","It was narrated from Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, bequeathed four thousand to the mothers of his children, four thousand to each of them women."
"3314","Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, justified the will of a thirteen-year-old boy."
"3315","Abu Ishaq said: A seven-year-old boy of a tribe made a will, so Qazi Shareeh said: If the will is valid, it is permissible. Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I like this opinion, but the judges do not accept it."
"3316","Abu Ishaq bin Isma'il narrated that he was with Qazi Shareeh, who validated the will of Abbas bin Ismail bin Murshad for the midwife of Ahl al-Hira, at that time Abbas was a child."
"3317","Abu Ishaq said: Qazi Shareeh said: When the child avoids (falling into) the well, his will is valid."
"3318","It was narrated from Abu Ishaq that a boy from his tribe whose name was Murshid and his (milk) teeth had fallen out, he bequeathed forty dirhams to his midwife from among the people of Hira."
"3319","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm reported that the time of death of a boy in Madinah was approaching, his heirs were in Syria, people mentioned him to Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and said that he was near death, can he make a will? Sayyiduna Umar ordered that he could bequeath, so he bequeathed a well called Bir Jashm which was sold by its owners for thirty thousand. Abu Bakr mentioned: The boy was ten or twelve years old."
"3320","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is permissible for a child to bequeath one-third or less of his wealth, and if he is healthy, his guardian can prevent the child from bequeathing for fear of poverty and starvation, but at the time of death, he is not allowed to prevent him from bequeathing."
"3321","It was narrated from Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, that a girl was brought to Abdullah bin Utbah who had made a will."
"3322","It was narrated from Abu Bakr that Salim Ghasani died when he was ten or twelve years old. He bequeathed his well worth thirty thousand. Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) made it valid. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: People call Salim Ghasani Amr bin Salim (that is, the correct one is Amr bin Salim and not Salim Ghasani)."
"3323","Abdullah and Muhammad narrated on the authority of his father Abu Bakr (bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm) in the same way (as passed above) except that one of them said: The boy was thirteen years old, and the other said: Before reaching adulthood (made a will). Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \"Un Ibneeh\" means the two sons of Abu Bakr (Abdullah and Muhammad)."
"3324","Muammar narrated that (Imam) Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, used to say that a will (of a child) is not permissible except for something that has no status. That is, the boy's will will not be effective before puberty."
"3325","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Divorce of a child is not permissible, nor is his will, gift, charity, or freedom until he reaches adulthood."
"3326","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It is not permissible to divorce a child, nor to set him free, nor to bequeath him, nor to buy or sell him, nor anything else."
"3327","(Maqtu' Hadith) Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Hammam narrated from Qatadah, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, who said: \"No divorce and no will is valid except from a person of sound mind, except for the intoxicated one—meaning the drunkard—for his divorce is valid, and his back is to be struck (as a punishment).\""
"3328","Yahya bin Abi Ishaq said: I asked Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman and Muawiya bin Qara about the will of a man who says that all my slaves are free and one of his slaves is a runaway."
"3329","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that Sayyidna Umar (RA) made a will for the mother of the believers, Sayyida Hafsa (RA)."
"3330","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Safiyya (RA) made a will for one of her Jewish relatives."
"3331","Abu Ishaq said: A seven-year-old boy of the tribe, whose name was Abbas bin Murshad, made a will to give forty dirhams to a Jewish midwife from among his family. Imam Abu Muhammad Darami (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I also say the same."
"3332","Hisham narrated from his father (Urwa bin Al-Zubayr) that Sayyidna Zubair bin Al-Awam (RA) dedicated his houses to his sons and made it a condition that they should not be sold or inherited, and he told one of his divorced daughters to stay in it and not harm this house, and that no one else should harm it, and a married daughter has no right to live in this house."
"3333","Narrated Makhool, may God have mercy on him: Should a man bequeath to spend a dinar in the way of Allah for a person, and the bequeather dies before the bequeather? He said: A will is valid for the heirs of the person for whom the will is made before it leaves the hands of the heirs of the testator. He also said: It is the responsibility of the heirs of the deceased to execute this will in the way of Allah."
"3334","On the authority of Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him: If a man makes a will for a person, and he dies before the testator (for whom the will is made), Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Such a will is permissible for the heirs of the legatee (i.e., for whom the will is made)."
"3335","Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i said: It was narrated to me that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to justify such a will. (i.e.) according to the words of Hasan, may God have mercy on him, he also said."
"3336","It was narrated from Nafi that a man came to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) and said, \"A man has bequeathed me to give a camel in the way of Allah, and this is not even the time of Jihad. Can I send it for Hajj?\" Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Hajj and Umrah are included in the way of Allah."
"3337","It was narrated from Waqid bin Muhammad bin Zayd bin Abdullah bin Umar that a man bequeathed his property to be spent in the cause of Allah. He said: Hajj to the House of Allah."
"3338","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, the person in whose chest there is nothing of the Holy Qur'an is like a deserted house.\""
"3339","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: This Holy Qur’an is the table of Allah Almighty, take it as much as you can, I know of no house so needy that it does not have some part of the Book of Allah, surely the heart that does not have some of the Book of Allah is desolate like the desolation of a house in which no one lives."
"3340","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Learn this Holy Quran, you will be rewarded with ten good deeds for each letter of its recitation."
"3341","Hafs bin Ghiyath Hanafi narrated that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may God be pleased with him) used to say: Verily, if the Holy Qur’an is recited in a house, it becomes spacious for the people of that household. It happens."
"3342","Uqbah bin Aamir says: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"If the Holy Qur'an is written on leather, and then thrown into the fire, it will not burn.\""
"3343","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Read the Qur'an, it will be a very good intercessor on the Day of Resurrection, he will say on the Day of Resurrection: O my Lord! Let him (the reciter of the Qur'an) be clothed with the jewel of dignity, so he will be adorned with the jewel of honor and dignity, then he will say: O Lord! Put him in the robe of dignity, so this person will be clothed in the robe of dignity, then he will intercede: O Lord! Make him wear the crown of glory, O Lord! Be satisfied with it, nothing is needed after your consent."
"3344","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: On the Day of Resurrection, the Holy Qur'an will come and intercede for its reciter and say: O Lord! Every laborer has his wages for his work, and I used to prevent him from pleasure and from sleeping, so honor him, it will be said: Stretch out your right hand and it will be filled with the pleasure of Allah, then it will be said: Stretch out your left hand and it will be filled with the pleasure of Allah, and he will be clothed with honor and honor, he will be adorned with the jewel of honor and on his (head) honor. will be crowned."
"3345","Abu Saleh said: The Holy Qur'an will intercede for its reciter, then he (the reciter) will be clothed with dignity, the Qur'an will say: O Lord! And increase, so the crown of honor will be worn, said then he will say: O Lord! And give him more, bless him more, Allah will grant him His pleasure. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Wahib bin Al-Ward said: Make the recitation of the Qur'an a knowledge, not (only) an action."
"3346","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Would any of you like to find three very fat pregnant camels grazing when he came to his house?\" He said: Indeed, O Messenger of Allah! (Every one of us likes him), said: \"So three verses which a man recites are better than three (fat pregnant) camels.\""
"3347","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Verily, this Qur’an is the table of Allah. Learn as much as you can from its table. Verily, this Qur’an is the rope of Allah, the light, the healing and the beneficent. It is a cause (of avoiding sins) for whoever holds it, and salvation for whoever follows it. He who walks on it will not go astray so that he has to seek permission, nor will it be crooked so that he will have to be straightened. The wonders are not going to end, and it will not get old by reading it again and again, read it, surely Allah will reward you for reciting it, there are ten good deeds for each letter, I do not say that Alm is one letter, but Al Lam and Meem are (separate letters)."
"3348","Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: One day, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, stood up to deliver the sermon. He, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, praised Allah and praised Him. Then he said: \"O people! I am a human being. The Messenger of my Lord (the angel of death) is near. Come and let me accept (his words). I am leaving two great things with you. The first is the Book of Allah, in it is guidance and light, so you are Allah's. Hold on to the Book and hold it firmly,\" so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised the Book of Allah and made it attractive, then said: \"And my Ahl al-Bayt, I remind you of Allah about my Ahl al-Bayt.\" He said this three times."
"3349","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This path is surrounded, the devils surround it (i.e. call to the path of misguidance) and they call out, O Abdullah (faithful narrations, O servants of Allah), this is the right path, so hold fast to the rope of Allah, and the rope of Allah is the Holy Qur’an."
"3350","Khalid bin Ma'dan said: Verily, the angels pray for those who recite the Qur'an and those who learn the Qur'an until they finish the surah, so the reciter and learner of the Qur'an should leave two verses and recite them at the end of the day so that the angels pray for the reciter and the learner from dawn to dusk."
"3351","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Al-Bahli (RA) used to say: Read the Qur'an, do not let these hanging books deceive you, because Allah will never punish the heart that has memorized the Qur'an."
"3352","The translation of this effect is the same as above. In some hadiths, it is \"waa' to the Qur'an\". That is, the heart that is the home of the Qur'an."
"3353","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Every teacher of literature wants his literature to be adopted, and the literature of Allah is the Holy Qur'an."
"3354","Abul Ahus said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) used to say: Verily, this is the table of Allah's Qur'an, and whoever comes upon it is safe and secure."
"3355","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: For the one who loves the Qur'an, there is glad tidings. (That means he should be happy.)"
"3356","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: For the one who loves the Qur'an, there is glad tidings. (That means he should be happy.)"
"3357","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu used to say: On the Day of Judgment, the Holy Qur'an will come and intercede for its reciter, and guide him to Paradise, testify for him, and drive him away from Hell."
"3358","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Some of the people belong to Allah.\" It was asked: Who are those people of Allah? He said: \"They are the people of the Qur'an\" (i.e. those who teach reading the Qur'an)."
"3359","Sayyiduna Ka'b, may God be pleased with him, said: Hold on to the Qur'an because it gives understanding to the mind, and is the light of wisdom, the fountainhead of knowledge, and it is the most recent book in relation to the nearness of God Almighty. Addressing in the Torah, God Almighty said: O Muhammad! I am about to reveal to you the Torah, a new book, which will open closed eyes, deaf ears, hearts veiled in ignorance."
"3360","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may God be pleased with him) said: This Holy Qur’an is a source of reward for you, a remembrance and a light for you, or else (if you don’t follow it) it is a disaster for you. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \"Yazakh\" means \"to pull away\"."
"3361","Ayyas bin Aamir says: Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may God be pleased with him) took my hand and said: If you live (you will see that) three types of people will read the Qur’an, one type will read the Qur’an for the sake of Allah, and one type will read the Qur’an for the sake of fighting (debate), and one type will read it for the sake of the world, and the one who reads it for the sake of evil will gain its meaning."
"3362","On the authority of Abu Qalaba, a man said to Sayyiduna Abul Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him: Your Ahl al-Zikr brothers of Kufa greet you."
"3363","Harith Al-Awur said: I entered the mosque and saw people talking, so I went to Sayyiduna Ali and said: Don't you see that people are talking while sitting in the mosque? He said: Are those people doing this? I said: Yes, Sayyiduna Ali said: Listen! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \"Tribulations will appear soon\", I asked: What is the way out of them? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The Book of Allah (i.e. the Qur’an is the means of avoiding them), in the Book of Allah there is news of those who have (passed) before you, and there is news of those who will come (in the world) after you, and it is a ruling between you (i.e. a ruling for those who have differences between you), it is clear, it is not a joke. I seek guidance, Allah will guide him astray, and it is the strong rope of Allah, and the remembrance of wisdom and wisdom, and the straight path, it is a book that cannot be twisted by human desires (Ahwa), and tongues cannot find in it, and the scholars do not get tired of it, and it does not become old by repeated reading, and its wonders do not end, and it is a book that when the jinn heard it. So it cannot be said without saying, \"We have heard a strange Qur'an.\" [Al-Jun 1/72], He who spoke according to it spoke the truth, and judged according to it he did justice, acted according to it he was rewarded, and whoever called to it was guided to the straight path.” O Harris, remember him."
"3364","On the authority of Harith al-Awur, Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: It was asked of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): After him, your ummah may be afflicted with temptations. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The way out of it is the honorable book of Allah (to which no falsehood can enter, neither from before it, nor from behind it, it is revealed by Allah, the Wise, the Virtuous... 42/41). It is the remembrance of wisdom, the light is clear, and the path is straight, in it is the news of the people before you and the news of those who will come after you, and it is the ruling (judgment) between you, it is clear, there is no joke, this is the Qur'an which the jinn heard and could not stop saying, \"We have heard such a strange Qur'an that guides to the right path.\" [Algin 1/72] \n, which does not grow old (that is, one does not tire of it) by repeated reading, its lessons do not cease, nor its wonders complete.\" Then Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Harith Awar: Remember this, O Awar."
"3365","This verse was narrated from Abraham, may God have mercy on him: . . . . .﴾» In [Al-Baqarah: 269/2], wisdom refers to the understanding of the Qur'an. Meaning: He who is given wisdom and understanding is given much goodness."
"3366","Mujahid said: «﴿Yuِـــــــــــَـــــــــــــــــــــــــــــــــرــــــــــــــــــــــــــــو, . . . . .﴾» [Al-Baqarah: 269/2] Allah bestows wisdom on whom He wills."
"3367","Khaysma said to his wife: Beware! Do not allow those who drink alcohol to enter my house, even though the Quran is recited in it every three days."
"3368","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: What prevents one of you from sitting on his bed and reciting three verses of the Qur'an when he returns home after fulfilling his needs in the market or?"
"3369","Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The best among you is the one who reads and teaches the Qur'an.\""
"3370","(Marfūʿ hadith) Hajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to me, ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad informed me, he said: I heard Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Rahmān al-Sulamī, from ʿUthmān, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \"Indeed, the best among you are those who learn the Qur’an or teach it.\" He said: Abū ʿAbd al-Rahmān recited during the caliphate of ʿUthmān until the time of al-Hajjāj, and he said: \"That is what has seated me in this place.\""
"3371","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrated from his father, the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \"The best of you is the one who learned and taught the Qur'an.\""
"3372","On the authority of Sayyidna Sa'd bin Ubada, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever forgets the Qur'an after reciting (memorizing) it, he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with his hand cut off.\" (ie will be found empty handed or speechless). Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Isa: Ibn Fayed."
"3373","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Recite the Qur'an frequently before it is lifted. The people said: These books will be lifted, but how will (the Qur'an) be lifted from the chests of the people? He replied that a night will pass over them that they will be deprived of it and will forget to say La ilaha illa Allah and the words of Jahiliyyah will fall into poetry and this will happen when the word of Allah will come true on them."
"3374","Salam bin Abi Muti'i said: Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, used to say: Settle your hearts, and settle your houses. The narrator said: I think their aim was to settle with the Qur'an."
"3375","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) said: One night will pass over the Holy Qur'an in such a way that not a single verse will remain in the Mushaf or remain in anyone's heart, rather it will be removed."
"3376","Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: Whoever sits down for the sake of the Qur'an, then stands up, he will get up with excess or loss. Then he recited this verse: (Al-Isra': 82/17) That is, \"This Qur'an which We are sending down is a complete healing and mercy for the believers, and the wrongdoers are not harmed except by harm.\""
"3377","Thabit bin Ajlan Ansari said: It was said that Allah intends to punish the people of the earth, but when He hears the children being taught wisdom, He changes His intention. Marwan said: Wisdom refers to the teaching of the Qur'an."
"3378","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) said: In the hearts of some people, the Holy Qur'an will become old just like cloth becomes old, people will read it but will not find pleasure in it, such people will wear the skin of sheep on melting hearts, their actions will be greedy, and there will be no fear of God in them. If we do, we will be forgiven because we do not associate anything with Allah."
"3379","On the authority of Sayyidina Abdullah bin Masoud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is very bad for one of you to say that I have forgotten such and such a verse (rather, it should be said that) I have been forgotten, and continue reciting the Holy Qur'an, for it is more distant in the hearts of men than the flight of a camel.\""
"3380","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Read the Book of Allah and protect it (ie, repeat it repeatedly), mutter to it and hold fast to it. By the One in Whose hand is my life (or he said: By the One in whose hand is the life of Muhammad) because it is more distant than the flight of a camel.\""
"3381","Sayyiduna Uqba bin Aamir (RA) narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Read the Book of Allah, remember it, cling to it, and murmur to it. By the One in Whose Hand is my life, He is more eager to forget than a camel to run away.\" (That is, just as the camel runs away, the Holy Quran also disappears from the hearts)."
"3382","It was narrated from Ibn Abi Malika that Sayyiduna Ikrama bin Abi Jahl (RA) used to put the Holy Qur'an on his face and say: This is the book of my Lord, this is the book of my Lord."
"3383","Thabit stated that Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laili used to recite the Qur'an after Fajr prayer until sunrise. The narrator said: And Thabit used to do the same."
"3384","Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: This verse: “But those who believe, then they know that it is the truth from their Lord. . . . . .﴾» [Al-Baqarah: 26/2] means that the believers know that this is the speech of the Most Merciful."
"3385","Atiya bin Qays said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"No one's speech is greater in the sight of Allah than his own speech, and the servants do not recite any speech that is more beloved to Allah than his own speech.\""
"3386","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to present himself to the pilgrims in Arafat during the Hajj and say: \"Can any man take me under the protection of his people? Because the Quraysh have stopped me from preaching the word of my Lord.\""
"3387","Abu al-Za'ra' said: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This Qur'an is the word of Allah, do not be deceived by making it according to your wishes."
"3388","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Whoever was distracted by the recitation of the Holy Qur’an in questioning Me and remembering Me, I gave him a good reward from the questioners, and the greatness of the word of God is over all words as the greatness and greatness of God is over His creation.”"
"3389","Shahr bin Hushab said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The superiority of the speech of Allah over the speech of the creatures is like the superiority of Allah over His creatures.\""
"3390","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The Holy Qur'an is dearer to Allah than the heavens and the earth and what is between them.\""
"3391","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jundab (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \"Recite the Qur'an until your heart fills, then stand up when your heart fills up (i.e. dismiss the assembly and stop the recitation).\""
"3392","Sayyiduna Jundab bin Abdullah (RA) said: Read the Qur'an until your heart touches it, then stop reciting it when you start to faint."
"3393","The translation of this hadith of Sayyiduna Jandab (RA) has been given above."
"3394","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There are some people who are given faith but not the Qur'an, and some of them who receive the Qur'an but do not gain faith, and some who receive both the Qur'an and faith, and some who are neither given faith nor the Qur'an. Then giving his example, Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: The example of the one who was given faith and did not get the Qur'an is like a date, which tastes sweet but does not smell, and the example of the one who received the Qur'an and did not get faith is like that of medicine, the smell of which is good and the taste is bitter, and the example of the one who got both the Qur'an and faith is like an orange (sweet lemon) which has a good aroma and taste, and the example of the one who did not get the Qur'an and faith is like that of Indrain. It has a bitter taste and no fragrance."
"3395","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The example of a believer who recites the Qur’an is like an orange whose taste is delicious and its aroma is excellent, and the example of a believer who does not recite the Qur’an is like a date palm, which tastes good but has no fragrance, and the example of a hypocrite who recites the Qur’an is like a rehana (flower) whose aroma is good but its taste is good.” It is bitter, and the hypocrite who does not even recite the Qur'an is like Indrayan whose taste is bitter, and there is no fragrance in it."
"3396","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The example of the one who was given faith but not the Qur’an is like a date palm, which tastes delicious but has no fragrance, and the example of the one who was given the Qur’an and did not believe is like a flower whose fragrance is good but the taste is bitter, and the example of the one who was given both the Qur’an and the faith is like an orange whose taste is delicious and the smell is excellent, and that The example of one who was not given the Qur'an or faith is like the one who has bad smell and bad taste."
"3397","Amir bin Wathlah narrated that Nafi bin Abdul Harith met Sayyiduna Umar in Isfan, whom Sayyiduna Umar had appointed as ruler of Makkah, (Amir al-Mu'minin). Nafi said: I have made Ibn Abzai my deputy over them. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: Who is Ibn Abzai? He said: He is one of our freed slaves. Sayyiduna Umar said: You have made Molly a caliph over them. He said: O Ameerul Momineen! He is a reciter of the Qur'an and a scholar of duties. Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Verily, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Verily, Allah will exalt many nations with the blessing of this Qur'an and subjugate others.\""
"3398","Khalid bin Madan said: Verily, the one who recites the Qur'an has one reward and the one who listens to the Qur'an has a double reward."
"3399","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever listens to a verse of the Holy Qur'an carefully, it will be a light for him."
"3400","On the authority of Sayyida Aisha, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, the person who recites the Qur'an and is an expert in it (i.e. Hafiz) will be with the noble, good writing angels, and the one who recites the Qur'an and finds it difficult to recite the Qur'an, he will have a double reward.\" (One reward for reciting the Qur'an and one reward for enduring hardship in recitation)."
"3401","Wahib al-Zhamari said: The person to whom Allah has blessed the Qur'an and recites it morning and evening, and acts on what is in it, and dies only on obedience and obedience, such a person will be raised by Allah on the Day of Resurrection with \"Safarah\" and \"Ahakm\". Saeed bin Abdul Aziz said: \"Safarah\" means: angels, and \"rules\" means prophets. Wahib said: And whoever is eager to memorize the Holy Qur'an but forgets it and does not leave it (i.e. keeps reading), he will get a double reward. But it is like the vulture (vulture) is heavy on all the birds, or like the superiority of a green pasture on the (barren) land around it, then when the Day of Resurrection will come, it will be said: Where are those who used to recite my book and did not care about grazing cattle (i.e. the busyness of the world)? Such a person will be given Paradise and eternity therein. Al-Mulk will be clothed, they will both say: O our Lord, our deeds were not so good, Allah will say: Yes, it is because your son used to recite my book."
"3402","Abdul Malik bin Umayr said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"In Surah Fatiha there is healing from every disease.\""
"3403","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed bin Al-Maali Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me. . . . . . . When Allah and the Messenger call you, answer yes.\" Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Before leaving the mosque, I will tell you the greatest surah of the Qur'an.\" And when he, peace and blessings of God be upon him, intended to leave, he said: \"The greatest surah is Alhamdulillah, Lord of the Worlds (i.e. Surah Fatiha), which is the seventh and the greatest Qur'an that has been given to you.\""
"3404","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \"Fatihah-ul-Katab is the seven-fold.\""
"3405","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There was no surah like it revealed in the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel and the Qur'an, (what he meant by Umm al-Qur'an) is the seven-fold and the great Qur'an that was given to me.\""
"3406","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Praise be to Allah, the Mother of the Qur'an, the Mother of the Book, and the seven bladders.\""
"3407","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: In a house where Surah Al-Baqarah is recited, Satan flees by expelling the wind."
"3408","Khalid bin Ma'dan said: Learning Surah Al-Baqarah is a source of good and blessing, and abandoning it is a source of regret and regret. Magicians do not have the strength to resist it. This is the tent of the Qur'an."
